   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "A particle moves along a line, and its position \\( s(t) \\) satisfies the differential equation \\( \\frac{ds}{dt} = e^{2 t} \\) with \\( s(0) = 1 \\). Writing the particular solution as \\( s(t) = 1 + \\int_{0}^{t} v(u) \\, du \\), where \\( v \\) is the given rate, find the exact value of \\( s(\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 5
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The accumulation form of the solution is \\( s(t) = 1 + \\int_{0}^{t} v(u) \\, du \\), with an antiderivative of the rate \\( \\frac{e^{2 t}}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Exp",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  "t"
               ]
            ],
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The initial value fixes the constant term: at \\( t = 0 \\) the integral is 0, so \\( s(0) = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Evaluate the integral: \\( \\int_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}} v(u) \\, du = 4 \\).",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( s(\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}) = 1 + 4 = 5 \\).",
         "mathjson": 5
      }
   ],
